# R113: a rachana reference beside an operator is refused - E_RACHANA_GANIT. Up to v292 `p == q`
# compared two addresses (0 here, though both records hold 3), `p < q` ordered them and `p + q` added them.
# Compare the fields: `p.x == q.x`. What `p == q` will mean is the same record (identity); until then it is
# refused, as a kosh (E_KOSH_GANIT) and a mala (E_MALA_GANIT) are.
rachana Bindu = { x, y }

mukhya() {
    vitti p = nirmmita(16)
    vitti q = nirmmita(16)
    p.x = 3
    q.x = 3
    likha(p.x == q.x)
    likha(p == q)
}
